# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stays Fixed
#
# The one thing people get wrong: only the EVIDENCE is ignored, never the
# PROMISE. Approved pictures, guards, markers and recorded fixtures are the
# whole point of the tool and they all belong in git — without them a fresh
# checkout has nothing to compare against and every screen comes back "new".
#
# Ignored (thrown away and rewritten on every run):
#   .staysfixed/results/    the photos this run took, plus its diff images
#   .staysfixed/report.html the side-by-side page built from those photos
#
# Committed (do NOT add these to this file):
#   .staysfixed/approved/   the approved pictures a human said yes to
#   .staysfixed/guards/     one check per bug that was already fixed
#   .staysfixed/markers/    the known-good points a regression is traced to
#   .staysfixed/fixtures/   recorded network replies, so runs match
#   .staysfixed/history.json the flake register
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.staysfixed/results/
.staysfixed/report.html

# The example projects the test suite drives get the same treatment.
fixtures/**/.staysfixed/results/
fixtures/**/.staysfixed/report.html

# Run records this tool writes about the project it is checking. Machine-local state,
# never source — and a test that passed a bare string to openStore once wrote a scratch
# product's records in here and got them committed.
.staysfixed/v2/
